From de18604882d7fad43b4c1db5330deb8828a1c2b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:40:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Remove trailing newline from render device path

DdiMedia_GetDeviceFD()'s no-FD fallback built the device path with
sprintf(device_name, "/dev/dri/renderD%d\n", ...) -- a stray
newline baked into the format string. open() is called with the
literal path '/dev/dri/renderD128\n', which never exists, so
DdiMediaUtil_OpenGraphicsAdaptor() always fails (ENOENT) even after
DdiMedia_SelectIntelDevice() correctly found a candidate device.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 media_driver/linux/common/ddi/media_libva.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media_driver/linux/common/ddi/media_libva.cpp b/media_driver/linux/common/ddi/media_libva.cpp
index 7c8fbff78..9d32c0355 100755
--- a/media_driver/linux/common/ddi/media_libva.cpp
+++ b/media_driver/linux/common/ddi/media_libva.cpp
@@ -1715,7 +1715,7 @@ VAStatus DdiMedia_GetDeviceFD (
             return VA_STATUS_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER;
         }
         char device_name[64];
-        sprintf(device_name, "/dev/dri/renderD%d\n", device_id + 128);
+        sprintf(device_name, "/dev/dri/renderD%d", device_id + 128);
         pDRMState->fd = DdiMediaUtil_OpenGraphicsAdaptor((char *)device_name);
         if (pDRMState->fd < 0) {
             DDI_ASSERTMESSAGE("DDI: Still failed to open the graphic adaptor, return failure");
-- 
